# Next.js Patterns

**Trigger**: Auto-applied to `app/` directory files and `proxy.ts`.

> **Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing any code.** This project uses Next.js 16.2.6 with breaking changes from earlier versions. Heed deprecation notices.

## Server vs Client Components

> **Server/Client Component Classification**: See [react-components.mdc](.cursor/rules/react-components.mdc) for authoritative classification rules, third-party context providers, and module-level JSX patterns. This file covers Next.js-specific patterns only.

**Default to Server Components.** Only add `'use client'` when the component requires browser APIs or interactivity.

## Route Handlers (API Routes)

**File convention**: `app/api/[resource]/route.ts`

**Always export named HTTP method functions** (`GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE`, `PATCH`):

```typescript
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { z } from 'zod';
import { prisma } from '@/lib/prisma';
import { logger } from '@/lib/logger';

const createSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  email: z.string().email(),
});

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  try {
    const body = await req.json();
    const parsed = createSchema.safeParse(body);

    if (!parsed.success) {
      return NextResponse.json(
        { error: 'Invalid request body', details: parsed.error.flatten() },
        { status: 400 }
      );
    }

    const resource = await prisma.resource.create({ data: parsed.data });
    return NextResponse.json({ data: resource }, { status: 201 });
  } catch (error) {
    log.error('api.request.error', { error: String(error) });
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: 'Internal server error' },
      { status: 500 }
    );
  }
}
```

**Validate all inputs with Zod**. Never trust `req.json()` output.

**Use standard HTTP status codes**: 200/201 success, 400 bad request, 401 unauthorized, 403 forbidden, 404 not found, 409 conflict, 500 internal error.

**Response shape consistency**:

```typescript
// Success
{ data: { ... } }
// Error
{ error: 'message', details?: { ... } }
```

## Route Groups

**Use route groups `(name)` for layout scoping without URL segments**:

```
app/
  (auth)/
    layout.tsx        # Shared auth layout
    login/page.tsx
    register/page.tsx
  (dashboard)/
    layout.tsx        # Shared dashboard layout
    page.tsx
    settings/page.tsx
```

Route groups are stripped from URLs. `app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` maps to `/login`.

## Proxy (Next.js 16)

**In Next.js 16, `middleware.ts` is renamed to `proxy.ts` and exports `proxy` instead of `middleware`**.

**Keep proxy fast and stateless**. Do not run database queries in the proxy. Use the `auth()` wrapper pattern from Auth.js v5 for session checks:

```typescript
// proxy.ts
import NextAuth from "next-auth";
import { NextResponse, type NextRequest } from "next/server";
import authConfig from "./auth.config";

const { auth } = NextAuth(authConfig);

export const proxy = auth(async function proxy(request: NextRequest) {
  const session = await auth();
  if (!session?.user) {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL("/login", request.url));
  }
  return NextResponse.next();
});

export const config = {
  matcher: ["/((?!api|_next/static|_next/image|favicon.ico|.*\\..*).*)"],
};
```

**Exclude API routes, static assets, and image files** from proxy via the matcher.

## Data Fetching

**Server Components fetch data directly** — no `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps`:

```typescript
// GOOD — Server Component
export default async function Page() {
  const posts = await prisma.post.findMany({
    where: { userId },
    orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
  });
  return <PostList posts={posts} />;
}
```

**For external API calls in Server Components**, use `fetch` with cache configuration:

```typescript
const data = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
  next: { revalidate: 3600 }, // Cache for 1 hour
});
```

**Never pass `req` or `res` to Server Components** — use `headers()`, `cookies()`, and `searchParams` from `next/headers` instead.

## Authentication Integration

**Use the `auth()` helper from the auth config in Server Components and Route Handlers**:

```typescript
// Server Component
import { auth } from '@/lib/auth';

export default async function ProtectedPage() {
  const session = await auth();
  if (!session?.user) {
    return redirect('/login');
  }
  // ...
}
```

```typescript
// Route Handler
import { auth } from '@/lib/auth';

export async function GET() {
  const session = await auth();
  if (!session?.user) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 });
  }
  // ...
}
```

**Do not read session from cookies directly in route handlers** — always use the `auth()` helper.

### SessionProvider in Root Layout

`SessionProvider` from `next-auth/react` uses `useContext` internally and **must** live in a Client Component. Never import it directly in `app/layout.tsx` (a Server Component).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — use a Client Component wrapper in layout
// app/layout.tsx (Server Component)
import { Providers } from '@/components/providers'; // has "use client"

export default async function RootLayout({ children }) {
  const session = await auth(); // can be null for unauthenticated users
  return (
    <Providers session={session}>
      {children}
    </Providers>
  );
}
```

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — providers.tsx (Client Component)
"use client";
import { SessionProvider } from "next-auth/react";
import type { Session } from "next-auth";

export function Providers({ children, session }: { children: React.ReactNode; session?: Session | null }) {
  return (
    <SessionProvider session={session ?? undefined}>
      {children}
    </SessionProvider>
  );
}
```

**Critical rules for SessionProvider**:
1. **Always render `SessionProvider`** — even when unauthenticated. The `signIn()` function from `next-auth/react` requires `SessionProvider` context to work, even on login pages.
2. **Pass `undefined` not `null`** — when `auth()` returns `null` (unauthenticated), convert to `undefined` before passing to `SessionProvider`. Passing `null` can cause context initialization issues.
3. **Never conditionally skip `SessionProvider`** — auth layouts, login pages, and public pages all need the `SessionProvider` context for `signIn()` and `useSession()` to function.

## Form Handling

**Server Actions for forms when possible** (Next.js 16 preferred pattern):

```typescript
// Server Action in a 'use server' file or component
'use server';

import { z } from 'zod';
import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache';
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation';

const formSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1),
});

export async function createItem(formData: FormData) {
  const parsed = formSchema.safeParse(Object.fromEntries(formData));
  if (!parsed.success) {
    return { error: 'Invalid input' };
  }
  await prisma.item.create({ data: parsed.data });
  revalidatePath('/dashboard');
  redirect('/dashboard');
}
```

**Client-side forms use `onSubmit` with async handlers**: See `app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` for the pattern.

## Error Boundaries

**Use `error.tsx` and `not-found.tsx` files per route segment** for graceful error handling:

```typescript
// app/dashboard/error.tsx
'use client';

export default function Error({ error, reset }: { error: Error; reset: () => void }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Something went wrong</h2>
      <button onClick={reset}>Try again</button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Layout Composition

**Layouts accept `children` and persist across navigations**:

```typescript
export default function AuthLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <div className="flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center p-4">
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Pass data from parent layouts to child pages via React Context or props, not server fetches inside nested layouts.**
